• The copy filter has to rejoin paragraphs like this one,
  which is deliberately long enough that the terminal user
  interface must wrap it at least twice at eighty columns,
  while keeping every word intact.

  1. First numbered item, which is also long enough to wrap
     onto a second line when the pane is narrow.

  2. Second item.
      • Nested bullet that runs on for quite a while so that
        it too wraps onto a continuation line.

      • Short nested bullet.

  • A plain bullet with a path: /home/user/projects/some-
    really-long-directory-name/src/components/widget.tsx

  • See https://example.com/a/very/long/url/path/that/keeps/
    going/and/going/until/it/wraps?query=1&b=2

  for f in *.txt; do printf '%s\n' "$f"; done | sort | uniq
  -c | sort -rn | head -n 20 # a long code line that must
  not be joined
  echo second line

   Name     Description
  ━━━━━━━  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
   alpha    The first entry in the table, with a fairly
            long description cell
  ───────  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
   beta     Second

  这是一个很长的中文段落，用来测试宽字符在终端换行边界上的处
  理是否正确，以及复制时是否能够正确地重新连接成一个段落而不
  丢失任何字符。

  Emoji check 🎉 with a sentence that keeps going so the
  emoji might land near the wrap boundary 🚀 and then more
  words follow here.
